      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Sociological literature suggests East Asian cultural socialization often emphasizes collectivism, leading to a prioritization of group harmony and indirect communication under stress. Conversely, Mediterranean cultures frequently value expressive individualism and direct confrontation, which can manifest as more assertive or emotionally open responses in conflict. Therefore, East Asian leaders might prioritize maintaining social equilibrium, while Mediterranean leaders may lean toward direct resolution and emotional articulation in high-stress interpersonal situations.",
